1
00:00:30,279 --> 00:00:31,864
The Grid.

2
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:35,493
A digital frontier.

3
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:39,622
I tried to picture
clusters of information

4
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:41,874
as they moved
through the computer.

5
00:00:43,125 --> 00:00:45,378
What did they look like?

6
00:00:45,461 --> 00:00:47,630
Ships? Motorcycles?

7
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,967
Were the circuits like freeways?

8
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:54,637
I kept dreaming of a world
I thought I'd never see.

9
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:58,933
And then, one day...

10
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:03,479
-You got in.
-That's right, man. I got in.

11
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:42,018
And the world was more
beautiful than I ever dreamed

12
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:44,770
and also more dangerous
than I ever imagined.

13
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:46,606
Hop in bed, now, kiddo.

14
00:01:48,065 --> 00:01:50,860
-Now, I met a brave warrior.
-Tron.

15
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:53,571
Bom-ba-bom-bom bom!

16
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,197
Tron!

17
00:01:55,531 --> 00:01:58,326
-He fights for the users.
-He sure does.

18
00:01:58,367 --> 00:02:02,580
Oh, man, he showed me things
that no one had ever imagined.

19
00:02:02,663 --> 00:02:06,208
There were these disk battles
fought in spectacular arenas.

20
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:09,045
Cycles that raced
on ribbons of light.

21
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:11,589
It was so radical.

22
00:02:11,672 --> 00:02:13,841
-And together...
-You built the Grid.

23
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:17,637
We built a new grid
for programs and users.

24
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:20,056
Now, I couldn't be
in there all the time,

25
00:02:20,139 --> 00:02:25,227
so I created a program in
my own image that could think.

26
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,396
Like you, and me.

27
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:31,359
And I called him Clu.

28
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:35,237
-Codified Likeness Utility.
-That's right.

29
00:02:35,946 --> 00:02:39,241
And Clu, Tron and I,
we built the system,

30
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:42,286
where all information
was free and open.

31
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:44,538
Beautiful.

32
00:02:46,874 --> 00:02:49,377
And then, one day,

33
00:02:50,419 --> 00:02:52,254
something happened.

34
00:02:54,965 --> 00:02:58,511
Something extraordinary.

35
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,973
A miracle.

36
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,104
What was it?

37
00:03:09,397 --> 00:03:12,191
That'll have to
wait till next time.

38
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:14,276
I gotta get to work.

39
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,861
I wanna go with you, Dad.

40
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:20,741
Yeah, well, one day you will.

41
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:22,284
I promise.

42
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:25,371
-To the Grid?
-Good night, Sam.

43
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:31,711
Hey, what do you say tomorrow
you and I hit the arcade?

44
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:34,505
You can have a crack at
the old man's high score.

45
00:03:34,588 --> 00:03:37,133
First game's on me.

46
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:41,512
Can we play doubles?
On the same team?

47
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,517
We're always on the same team.

48
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:10,124
Good evening. Our lead story.

49
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:14,962
ENCOM CEO and video game
icon Kevin Flynn has disappeared.

50
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:18,090
He was best known for designing
Tron and Space Paranoids,

51
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:20,926
the two bestselling
video games in history.

52
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:24,180
Flynn took ownership
of ENCOM in 1982

53
00:04:24,221 --> 00:04:27,641
as the company skyrocketed
to the top of the tech industry.

54
00:04:27,683 --> 00:04:32,021
But things changed in 1985 with
the untimely death of Flynn's wife,

55
00:04:32,104 --> 00:04:34,648
the mother of his
young son, Sam.

56
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:36,692
Recently, ENCOM board members

57
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,027
have been troubled by reports

58
00:04:38,110 --> 00:04:41,113
of Flynn's erratic, even
obsessive, behavior.

59
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:44,909
With Flynn missing, the
company is now in chaos.

60
00:04:44,992 --> 00:04:47,203
This afternoon, ENCOM's board

61
00:04:47,286 --> 00:04:50,498
moved to seize control from
Flynn's partner, Alan Bradley,

62
00:04:50,539 --> 00:04:53,542
vowing to return the
company to profitability.

63
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:58,881
Loyal to the end, Bradley maintains
his belief that Flynn is not missing

64
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:01,550
and is instead
pursuing his dream of

65
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:05,095
“a digital frontier to reshape
the human condition.”

66
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,225
In there is a new world.

67
00:05:09,266 --> 00:05:11,477
In there is our future.

68
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:15,856
In there is our destiny.

69
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,572
Even Flynn's most
ardent supporters

70
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:26,075
are now acknowledging
a difficult truth.

71
00:05:26,116 --> 00:05:28,911
Kevin Flynn may
have simply run away.

72
00:05:29,286 --> 00:05:32,039
And while Flynn's loyalists
hope for his imminent return,

73
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:35,918
there is perhaps no one who wishes it
to happen more than young Sam Flynn,

74
00:05:36,043 --> 00:05:40,172
now in the care of his grandparents,
and heir to an empire in turmoil.

75
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:43,843
He's coming. He promised.

76
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:45,928
-Sam, you have to eat.
-Let go of me!

77
00:05:46,011 --> 00:05:47,304
Sam?

78
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:50,641
What will become of Flynn's
legacy and the future of ENCOM

79
00:05:50,724 --> 00:05:51,934
will most likely depend

80
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:55,354
on what becomes of this
now orphaned little boy.

81
00:05:57,439 --> 00:05:59,567
Sam! Come back!

82
00:06:08,784 --> 00:06:10,911
All cycle units, stand by.

83
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:53,370
All units, stand by.

84
00:07:54,264 --> 00:07:56,016
Now that is a big door.

85
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,393
Welcome, everybody.

86
00:07:57,726 --> 00:08:01,021
Please settle. I know it's
late, so I'll skip the pleasantries

87
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:04,817
and hand things over to our
chairman, Richard Mackey.

88
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,738
Thank you. Thank
you. Thank you, Claire.

89
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,409
Tonight I am pleased to announce

90
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:19,456
that ENCOM's last fiscal year
was our most profitable ever.

91
00:08:20,332 --> 00:08:21,417
Yes.

92
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:43,605
At midnight the 12th version
of our flagship operating system

93
00:08:43,647 --> 00:08:46,025
will hit the shelves
around the world.

94
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:49,903
I'm sure it comes as no
surprise whom we have to thank.

95
00:08:50,070 --> 00:08:52,072
The head of our
software design team,

96
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:57,119
a man whose father's own
notable history with ENCOM

97
00:08:57,202 --> 00:08:59,955
helped make this
company what it is today.

98
00:09:02,499 --> 00:09:04,960
Edward Dillinger. Well done.

99
00:09:05,377 --> 00:09:06,879
Well done.

100
00:09:10,841 --> 00:09:14,845
And this year, simultaneous to
the release of ENCOM OS-12,

101
00:09:15,554 --> 00:09:20,934
we will be making our debut
on Tokyo's Nikkei Index.

102
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:25,939
ENCOM's stock will now
trade around the world 24/7.

103
00:09:25,981 --> 00:09:28,567
Huh? Oh, yes.

104
00:09:52,382 --> 00:09:55,177
-Excuse me.
-Yes, Alan?

105
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:56,762
Given the prices

106
00:09:56,845 --> 00:10:00,516
that we charge to
students and schools,

107
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:04,186
what sort of improvements
have been made in Flynn...

108
00:10:04,686 --> 00:10:07,940
I mean, ENCOM OS-127?

109
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:14,488
This year we put
a "12" on the box.

110
00:10:15,405 --> 00:10:18,867
OS-12 is the most secure
operating system ever released.

111
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:23,622
The idea of sharing our
software or giving it away for free

112
00:10:24,164 --> 00:10:26,542
disappeared with Kevin Flynn.

113
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:42,224
I know you're here.

114
00:10:42,766 --> 00:10:44,726
Let's make this easy.

115
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:48,730
Come on, come on.

116
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,448
Freeze!

117
00:10:59,199 --> 00:11:00,284
Okay.

118
00:11:00,617 --> 00:11:02,119
If there are no more questions,

119
00:11:02,661 --> 00:11:05,747
I would like you to meet
our next blockbuster.

120
00:11:05,789 --> 00:11:08,584
ENCOM OS-12.

121
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:11,879
Whoa.

122
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,256
Still a few bugs.

123
00:11:14,339 --> 00:11:16,008
What's that? What is that?

124
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:22,097
Just bear with us one sec.

125
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,433
Make this go away now.

126
00:11:24,516 --> 00:11:27,477
Stop what you're doing.
Stop. Stop for one second.

127
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:31,648
...where ENCOM's chairman,
Richard Mackey, will be launching...

128
00:11:31,732 --> 00:11:35,110
-We go live in 30 seconds.
-He's on the roof!

129
00:11:35,152 --> 00:11:37,988
-Anyone know where the master file is?
-I do.

130
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:40,741
It's on the Web.

131
00:11:42,951 --> 00:11:44,661
We've got to stop this.

132
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:51,001
I've got to ring
that opening bell.

133
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,712
-Make this stop now.
-It's locked.

134
00:11:53,795 --> 00:11:56,715
Just shut it down.
Shut it down! Now!

135
00:11:56,798 --> 00:11:59,801
Relax, Mackey. Relax.

136
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:01,220
It's under control.

137
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:03,347
Relax? Our most valuable

138
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,975
and most secure operating
system is out there for free!

139
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:08,769
How am I supposed
to explain that?

140
00:12:08,810 --> 00:12:11,813
I don't know. Say it
was all part of the plan.

141
00:12:12,814 --> 00:12:14,983
A little gift from ENCOM.

142
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:19,154
Apparently, ENCOM Technology
is having some technical difficulties.

143
00:12:20,447 --> 00:12:23,659
Why don't we give them a
chance to sort things out?

144
00:12:50,727 --> 00:12:52,729
Hey, Dad.

145
00:12:52,854 --> 00:12:54,648
How you doing?

146
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:04,324
-Where you gonna run to now?
-Hey, you don't wanna do that.

147
00:13:04,366 --> 00:13:06,702
Didn't anyone tell
you? Stealing is wrong.

148
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:09,413
You can't steal what
was designed to be free.

149
00:13:09,496 --> 00:13:12,666
-Now I got you.
-Your boss is okay with this.

150
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:14,042
The hell he is.

151
00:13:14,459 --> 00:13:16,253
Your boss works for the CEO

152
00:13:16,336 --> 00:13:17,963
and the CEO works
for the shareholders.

153
00:13:18,046 --> 00:13:20,382
Do you know who the
biggest shareholder is?

154
00:13:21,341 --> 00:13:22,968
I don't know. Some kid.

155
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,890
You're Mr. Flynn?

156
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:32,269
Why?

157
00:13:32,894 --> 00:13:35,272
This is your father's company.

158
00:13:35,355 --> 00:13:38,900
-Not anymore.
-What? Hey. Hey, kid.

159
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:41,653
No!

160
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:54,791
Yeah.

161
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:57,586
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

162
00:14:02,090 --> 00:14:03,342
You kidding me?

163
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:08,055
-That's him! Get the team down here!
-There he is! Get him!

164
00:14:09,681 --> 00:14:11,224
What the...

165
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,643
Hey! No free ride!

166
00:14:14,269 --> 00:14:16,813
-Whoa!
-No free taxi!

167
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,815
You pay!

168
00:14:21,443 --> 00:14:24,029
-Whoa, whoa, whoa -No free ride!

169
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:36,625
Hold it right there. Freeze!

170
00:14:38,543 --> 00:14:41,963
Okay, boys. You got me.

171
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:43,840
Hey.

172
00:14:58,688 --> 00:15:00,816
-Hey, Karl.
-Hey, how you doing?

173
00:15:16,748 --> 00:15:19,167
Enjoy it, Marv. You earned it.

174
00:15:23,171 --> 00:15:25,006
Why are you in my
apartment, Alan?

175
00:15:26,883 --> 00:15:29,010
You don't answer your phone.

176
00:15:31,471 --> 00:15:33,432
-How you been, Sam?
-Oh, you know,

177
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:37,185
when I was 12, I appreciated the
surrogate-father thing. But come on.

178
00:15:37,936 --> 00:15:39,855
I got it all under control now.

179
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:42,357
Oh. Clearly!

180
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:43,835
You want to help me
with my homework?

181
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:45,235
Like old times? Have a catch?

182
00:15:47,612 --> 00:15:51,116
You know, you got a
pretty nice view here.

183
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:57,080
Heard you did a triple Axel
off of her a few hours ago.

184
00:15:58,123 --> 00:16:00,959
-Rough landing, huh?
-Could have been worse.

185
00:16:01,042 --> 00:16:03,879
I also thought your
message to the board

186
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,088
was very clever.

187
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,674
Did you like that?
That was Marv's idea.

188
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:16,099
Alan, are we really
going to do this again?

189
00:16:16,933 --> 00:16:20,061
Do I really look like I'm ready
to run a Fortune 500 company?

190
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,813
No.

191
00:16:22,063 --> 00:16:26,151
And truthfully, the company is
pretty happy with where you are, too.

192
00:16:26,526 --> 00:16:27,569
I bet.

193
00:16:27,652 --> 00:16:30,822
That way they can keep
doing whatever they want.

194
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:36,912
You know, I guess what I find
curious is the crazy charities,

195
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,498
the annual prank on the company.

196
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:42,459
You have an interesting way
of being disinterested, Sam.

197
00:16:42,542 --> 00:16:44,377
Why are you here, Alan?

198
00:16:47,714 --> 00:16:49,424
I was paged last night.

199
00:16:49,549 --> 00:16:51,760
Oh, man, still
rocking the pager?

200
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:53,428
Good for you.

201
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:57,933
Yeah, your dad once told me I
had to sleep with it, and I still do.

202
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:01,436
Page came from your
dad's office at the arcade.

203
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:07,609
-So?
-So?

204
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:11,404
That number's been
disconnected for 20 years.

205
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:16,368
Sam, two nights before he
disappeared, he came to my house.

206
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:19,120
"I've cracked it,"
he kept saying.

207
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:22,999
He was talking about genetic
algorithms, quantum teleportation.

208
00:17:23,124 --> 00:17:27,379
He said he was about to change
everything. Science, medicine, religion.

209
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:30,966
He wouldn't have left that, Sam.

210
00:17:34,010 --> 00:17:35,387
He wouldn't have left you.

211
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:39,140
Oh, Alan. You're the only
one who still believes that.

212
00:17:39,432 --> 00:17:42,310
He's either dead or
chilling in Costa Rica.

213
00:17:43,311 --> 00:17:44,938
Probably both.

214
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,148
Look, I'm sorry.

215
00:17:47,190 --> 00:17:49,734
I'm tired, and
I smell like jail.

216
00:17:50,443 --> 00:17:54,781
Let's just reconvene in another
couple of years, huh? What do you say?

217
00:17:58,785 --> 00:17:59,995
Here.

218
00:18:01,162 --> 00:18:03,582
These are the
keys to the arcade.

219
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:09,462
I haven't gone over there yet. I
thought you should be the one.

220
00:18:09,504 --> 00:18:12,924
Alan, you're acting like I'm gonna
find him sitting there working.

221
00:18:13,049 --> 00:18:16,845
Just, "Hey, kiddo.
Lost track of time."

222
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:22,517
Wouldn't that be something?

223
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:33,320
What?

224
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:50,934
You son of a gun.

225
00:22:31,766 --> 00:22:33,309
Flynn.

226
00:22:39,274 --> 00:22:40,525
Huh.

227
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:43,653
Let's try the back door.

228
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:49,117
What were you working on?

229
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:57,625
LaserControl.

230
00:22:58,418 --> 00:22:59,794
Okay.

231
00:23:40,376 --> 00:23:42,503
This isn't happening.

232
00:23:58,269 --> 00:24:00,188
Oh, man, this is happening.

233
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:10,698
Wait.

234
00:24:12,116 --> 00:24:14,369
This program has
no disk. Another stray.

235
00:24:14,452 --> 00:24:15,495
Hey, wait.

236
00:24:15,703 --> 00:24:18,331
Wait. I'm not a program!

237
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:49,237
He actually did it.

238
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:54,409
I'm on the Grid.

239
00:25:04,002 --> 00:25:07,380
Does the name Kevin
Flynn mean anything to you?

240
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:09,382
Be quiet if you want to live!

241
00:25:09,424 --> 00:25:11,718
Not the games, not the games,

242
00:25:11,759 --> 00:25:14,220
not the games, not the games...

243
00:25:14,262 --> 00:25:15,638
What's his problem?

244
00:25:18,599 --> 00:25:20,435
Not the games, not the...

245
00:26:07,648 --> 00:26:09,400
Rectify.

246
00:26:12,695 --> 00:26:14,322
Rectify.

247
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:20,745
-Games.
-No. Please!

248
00:26:20,828 --> 00:26:21,913
Rectify.

249
00:26:21,996 --> 00:26:24,999
You probably get this a lot,
but there's been a big mistake.

250
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:27,001
Games.

251
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:30,379
-Please, no, no.
-Whoa. Hey.

252
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:33,091
No! Erase me!

253
00:26:38,137 --> 00:26:40,181
No! Wait! Wait!

254
00:27:21,347 --> 00:27:24,392
Er, can somebody
tell me what the...

255
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,232
Hey, hey. It's got a zipper.

256
00:27:48,833 --> 00:27:50,334
He is different.

257
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:00,303
This can't be good.

258
00:28:10,104 --> 00:28:15,067
Attention, program. You
will receive an identity disk.

259
00:28:15,234 --> 00:28:20,781
Everything you do or learn
will be imprinted on this disk.

260
00:28:21,782 --> 00:28:25,786
If you lose your disk or
fail to follow commands,

261
00:28:25,828 --> 00:28:29,665
you will be subject to
immediate de-resolution.

262
00:28:35,838 --> 00:28:39,133
Mirroring complete. Disk
activated and synchronized.

263
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:40,676
Proceed to games.

264
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:44,138
Games?

265
00:28:47,975 --> 00:28:49,644
Where are you going?

266
00:28:56,567 --> 00:28:57,985
What am I supposed to do?

267
00:28:58,986 --> 00:29:00,821
Survive.

268
00:29:52,915 --> 00:29:56,627
All combatants,
prepare for disk wars.

269
00:29:56,711 --> 00:30:00,214
Disk wars! Disk wars!

270
00:30:01,132 --> 00:30:02,466
Disk wars!

271
00:30:03,551 --> 00:30:05,094
Disk wars!

272
00:30:06,345 --> 00:30:08,347
Disk wars!

273
00:30:34,332 --> 00:30:36,709
Platform 8.

274
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:39,003
I have a three-inch
version of you on my shelf.

275
00:30:39,086 --> 00:30:41,922
Combatants 3 and 11.

276
00:30:42,048 --> 00:30:43,799
Disk wars.

277
00:30:53,893 --> 00:30:56,187
You definitely didn't do that.

278
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:28,928
Damn it!

279
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:39,313
So that's how it is.

280
00:31:56,038 --> 00:31:59,417
Combatant 11, de-resolution.

281
00:32:00,292 --> 00:32:03,254
I won. Now let me out!

282
00:32:03,337 --> 00:32:07,216
Combatant 3, round one, victory.

283
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:10,052
No unusual activity on the Grid.

284
00:32:10,136 --> 00:32:11,679
Security sweeps and patrols

285
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:14,306
have been intensified.
Rectifier on schedule.

286
00:32:14,348 --> 00:32:18,269
Your initiative should be fully
operational within 12 cycles.

287
00:32:19,895 --> 00:32:22,440
Perhaps if you
were to include me

288
00:32:22,523 --> 00:32:27,153
in this initiative, I could
be of even greater service.

289
00:32:27,194 --> 00:32:31,490
Combatants 3 and 7, disk wars.

290
00:32:34,201 --> 00:32:35,870
Initiate.

291
00:32:38,998 --> 00:32:42,376
Yeah. I'm out.

292
00:32:49,216 --> 00:32:51,385
Combatant 3, victory.

293
00:32:56,390 --> 00:32:58,601
Combatant 3, violation.

294
00:32:59,727 --> 00:33:03,397
Combatant 6, de-resolution.

295
00:33:03,439 --> 00:33:05,524
What is that program?

296
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:08,068
Combatant 3,

297
00:33:08,152 --> 00:33:10,154
violation.

298
00:33:15,409 --> 00:33:17,536
Initiate final round.

299
00:33:21,999 --> 00:33:25,085
Combatant 3 versus Rinzler.

300
00:33:25,127 --> 00:33:27,713
Rinzler!

301
00:33:27,755 --> 00:33:29,340
Rinzler!

302
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:34,094
You gotta be kidding me.

303
00:33:34,637 --> 00:33:35,721
Rinzler!

304
00:33:37,264 --> 00:33:39,058
Rinzler!

305
00:33:39,767 --> 00:33:41,143
Rinzler!

306
00:33:42,478 --> 00:33:43,604
Rinzler!

307
00:33:44,647 --> 00:33:45,981
Rinzler!

308
00:33:53,948 --> 00:33:55,991
Come on. Is that even legal?

309
00:34:29,483 --> 00:34:32,403
Why do I feel like I
just got dumped on?

310
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:41,078
Come on. Huh? Come on.

311
00:35:23,621 --> 00:35:25,289
De-rez!

312
00:35:26,665 --> 00:35:28,292
De-rez!

313
00:35:29,209 --> 00:35:30,544
De-rez!

314
00:35:34,882 --> 00:35:37,009
User.

315
00:35:48,062 --> 00:35:50,814
Identify yourself, program.

316
00:35:52,066 --> 00:35:54,360
I'm not a program.

317
00:35:59,865 --> 00:36:01,450
Identify.

318
00:36:03,077 --> 00:36:05,537
My name is Sam Flynn.

319
00:36:09,833 --> 00:36:12,044
Bring him to me.

320
00:36:14,588 --> 00:36:15,673
Let me go.

321
00:36:19,593 --> 00:36:20,969
Freaks.

322
00:36:23,138 --> 00:36:24,181
Where am I?

323
00:36:27,059 --> 00:36:29,603
Am I on the Grid?

324
00:36:30,938 --> 00:36:32,564
Who are you?

325
00:36:38,112 --> 00:36:39,238
Dad.

326
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:41,573
Sam.

327
00:36:41,615 --> 00:36:44,785
Look at you, man.
Look at the size of you.

328
00:36:46,787 --> 00:36:50,457
-How did you get in here?
-I got your message.

329
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:53,502
Oh. So it's just you?

330
00:36:54,461 --> 00:36:55,462
Yeah.

331
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:59,425
Just you. Oh.

332
00:36:59,466 --> 00:37:02,261
Isn't this something?

333
00:37:02,302 --> 00:37:03,595
You look the same.

334
00:37:03,637 --> 00:37:06,807
A lot's happened, Sam. More
than you can imagine. Disk.

335
00:37:12,104 --> 00:37:13,772
Let's have a look.

336
00:37:29,663 --> 00:37:31,165
Got it.

337
00:37:31,665 --> 00:37:33,834
Hmm. I expected more.

338
00:37:37,504 --> 00:37:40,257
So, you were trapped in here.

339
00:37:40,340 --> 00:37:41,842
That's right.

340
00:37:45,012 --> 00:37:48,098
-And you're in charge.
-Right again. You're two for two.

341
00:37:48,891 --> 00:37:51,477
So can we just go home now?

342
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:54,772
Not in the cards.

343
00:37:55,856 --> 00:37:57,232
Not for you.

344
00:38:01,361 --> 00:38:03,697
That's a hell of a
way to treat your son.

345
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:07,534
Oh, that.

346
00:38:12,164 --> 00:38:14,708
I'm not your father, Sam.

347
00:38:16,543 --> 00:38:19,838
But I'm very, very
happy to see you.

348
00:38:23,091 --> 00:38:25,052
Clu.

349
00:38:27,763 --> 00:38:29,014
Where is he?

350
00:38:29,097 --> 00:38:31,225
What did you do to him?

351
00:38:31,308 --> 00:38:35,687
Same thing I'm going
to do to you, user.

352
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:00,671
Greetings, programs.

353
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:06,969
Oh, what an occasion
we have here before us.

354
00:39:07,553 --> 00:39:11,431
Because your rumors are true.

355
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:16,353
We do indeed have in our midst

356
00:39:16,436 --> 00:39:18,564
a user!

357
00:39:20,732 --> 00:39:23,443
A user.

358
00:39:25,779 --> 00:39:28,073
So, what to do?

359
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:33,453
What does this user deserve?

360
00:39:33,495 --> 00:39:35,873
Might I suggest perhaps
the challenge of the Grid?

361
00:39:43,005 --> 00:39:47,968
And who best to battle
this singular opponent?

362
00:39:49,303 --> 00:39:53,473
Perhaps one who has some
experience in these matters.

363
00:39:56,768 --> 00:39:58,604
Oh, yes, indeed, programs.

364
00:39:59,479 --> 00:40:01,982
Your liberator!

365
00:40:02,065 --> 00:40:03,692
Your luminary!

366
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:06,945
Your leader and maker!

367
00:40:08,655 --> 00:40:12,242
The one who vanquished
the tyranny of the user

368
00:40:12,951 --> 00:40:15,662
those many cycles before!

369
00:40:16,663 --> 00:40:19,249
I've been waiting
a long time for this.

370
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:22,920
Clu!

371
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:26,173
You wanna play? I'll play.

372
00:40:32,512 --> 00:40:33,847
Excellent words, sir.

373
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:37,434
Were you pleased
with my execution?

374
00:40:37,517 --> 00:40:40,312
The crowd seemed
quite energized.

375
00:40:41,813 --> 00:40:43,982
It wasn't meant for them.

376
00:40:56,912 --> 00:40:58,830
What's this?

377
00:40:58,872 --> 00:41:00,707
What do I do with this?

378
00:41:00,791 --> 00:41:02,876
I'll give you a hint.

379
00:41:03,710 --> 00:41:05,170
Not that.

380
00:41:15,013 --> 00:41:16,556
Grid is live.

381
00:41:16,598 --> 00:41:20,060
Initiate light cycle battle.

382
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:36,326
You got no chance, user.

383
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:39,621
Their bikes are faster
than ours. Use the levels.

384
00:41:44,918 --> 00:41:47,045
Now this I can do.

385
00:42:19,411 --> 00:42:20,871
Here we go.

386
00:43:26,853 --> 00:43:28,313
Come on. Come on!

387
00:43:44,621 --> 00:43:47,624
Hey! We gotta work together.

388
00:43:47,707 --> 00:43:49,709
It's the only way.

389
00:43:57,759 --> 00:44:00,345
That's it. You got me.

390
00:44:08,228 --> 00:44:09,646
Boo!

391
00:44:12,691 --> 00:44:14,025
-Whoo-hoo!
-Yeah!

392
00:44:14,067 --> 00:44:16,236
Now that's what
I'm talking about.

393
00:44:16,528 --> 00:44:19,072
Another customer. Let's go!

394
00:44:36,590 --> 00:44:38,049
Hang on, buddy, I'm coming.

395
00:44:47,142 --> 00:44:48,310
Come on.

396
00:45:01,948 --> 00:45:04,451
This is it. Come on.

397
00:45:33,980 --> 00:45:35,941
illegal combatant on the Grid.

398
00:45:35,982 --> 00:45:37,442
Get in.

399
00:45:37,484 --> 00:45:39,069
Illegal combatant on the Grid.

400
00:45:39,152 --> 00:45:40,320
Get in!

401
00:45:46,493 --> 00:45:49,746
System failure. Release Rinzler.

402
00:45:49,829 --> 00:45:51,831
Game on, old friend.

403
00:46:01,049 --> 00:46:04,344
-Who are you?
-Hang on.

404
00:46:32,289 --> 00:46:33,873
Pull up, man, you
can't make that!

405
00:46:43,425 --> 00:46:45,844
Made it.

406
00:46:54,894 --> 00:46:56,104
I'm Quorra.

407
00:47:01,568 --> 00:47:02,819
They're turning around.

408
00:47:02,902 --> 00:47:04,279
Not by choice.

409
00:47:04,362 --> 00:47:07,949
Their vehicles can't go off Grid.
They'll malfunction on this terrain.

410
00:47:08,033 --> 00:47:11,411
-What about us?
-Obviously not.

411
00:47:19,002 --> 00:47:21,921
-Where are you taking me?
-Patience, Sam Flynn.

412
00:47:22,756 --> 00:47:25,592
All your questions
will be answered soon.

413
00:47:34,059 --> 00:47:35,685
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

414
00:48:38,581 --> 00:48:40,667
Walt here.

415
00:48:44,003 --> 00:48:45,463
Quorra.

416
00:48:46,506 --> 00:48:48,508
I dreamed of Tron.

417
00:48:49,592 --> 00:48:51,636
First time in years.

418
00:48:52,095 --> 00:48:53,721
It's a sign.

419
00:48:55,014 --> 00:48:58,393
A sign, my dear
apprentice, of a weary soul.

420
00:48:59,519 --> 00:49:02,772
-I'm afraid something's happened.
-Something has happened.

421
00:49:04,065 --> 00:49:05,692
We have a guest.

422
00:49:07,110 --> 00:49:09,654
There are no guests, kiddo.

423
00:49:33,219 --> 00:49:35,305
Sam...

424
00:49:36,347 --> 00:49:38,725
Long time.

425
00:49:40,185 --> 00:49:43,062
You have no idea.

426
00:49:48,776 --> 00:49:51,404
You're... You're here.

427
00:49:55,450 --> 00:49:56,910
You're here.

428
00:49:57,785 --> 00:50:00,246
I'm here.

429
00:50:07,795 --> 00:50:09,380
You're big.

430
00:50:10,757 --> 00:50:12,592
You're...

431
00:50:13,301 --> 00:50:14,677
Old.

432
00:50:18,348 --> 00:50:20,642
How did you get here?

433
00:50:20,725 --> 00:50:23,228
Alan came over.

434
00:50:23,937 --> 00:50:25,688
Bradley.

435
00:50:25,772 --> 00:50:28,608
Yeah. He got your page.

436
00:50:28,650 --> 00:50:31,945
I found your office
under the arcade.

437
00:50:33,321 --> 00:50:34,822
Page...

438
00:50:35,949 --> 00:50:37,242
Oh, the page.

439
00:50:38,535 --> 00:50:40,161
Of course.

440
00:50:44,207 --> 00:50:46,334
Clu had him on
the light cycle grid.

441
00:50:46,417 --> 00:50:48,586
I intervened.

442
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:50,296
Oh.

443
00:50:52,382 --> 00:50:53,424
Dinner soon.

444
00:50:54,342 --> 00:50:56,803
We'll talk then.

445
00:51:10,733 --> 00:51:13,987
He never thought
he'd see you again.

446
00:51:16,155 --> 00:51:17,865
Yeah.

447
00:51:24,998 --> 00:51:29,377
Vintage. Flynn built it many
cycles ago for the games.

448
00:51:30,420 --> 00:51:33,339
It doesn't get out as
much as it used to,

449
00:51:33,381 --> 00:51:36,384
but it's still the fastest
thing on the Grid.

450
00:51:59,407 --> 00:52:00,950
Do you know it?

451
00:52:01,909 --> 00:52:07,040
His patience usually beats out
my more aggressive strategy.

452
00:52:11,336 --> 00:52:13,671
Flynn shared them with me.

453
00:52:13,713 --> 00:52:15,548
I've read them all.

454
00:52:15,715 --> 00:52:18,468
Oh. Light reading.

455
00:52:19,302 --> 00:52:20,970
Tolstoy.

456
00:52:21,054 --> 00:52:23,264
Dostoyevsky.

457
00:52:23,348 --> 00:52:25,892
I-Ching. Journey Without Goal.

458
00:52:26,809 --> 00:52:29,187
Must have a killer ending.

459
00:52:29,228 --> 00:52:31,439
Flynn is teaching me
about the art of the selfless,

460
00:52:31,522 --> 00:52:36,235
about removing oneself
from the equation.

461
00:52:36,319 --> 00:52:41,157
But between you and me,
Jules Verne is my favorite.

462
00:52:42,325 --> 00:52:44,869
-Do you know Jules Verne?
-Sure.

463
00:52:45,870 --> 00:52:48,414
What's he like?

464
00:52:57,840 --> 00:53:00,259
Your move, Flynn, come on.

465
00:53:01,135 --> 00:53:03,471
Come on!

466
00:53:25,326 --> 00:53:29,664
-How old are you now, Sam?
-You should be 27.

467
00:53:30,707 --> 00:53:32,709
Yes, 27.

468
00:53:32,792 --> 00:53:36,212
-Do you attend a college?
-Caltech.

469
00:53:37,547 --> 00:53:41,342
Caltech. My Alma mater.

470
00:53:41,426 --> 00:53:42,760
Yeah.

471
00:53:42,802 --> 00:53:44,470
Till I dropped out.

472
00:53:53,896 --> 00:53:55,106
Work?

473
00:53:55,732 --> 00:53:58,568
-Job? ENCOM? Are you...
-No.

474
00:54:00,820 --> 00:54:03,239
I check in once a year.

475
00:54:04,615 --> 00:54:06,784
-Wife, girlfriend?
-Dog.

476
00:54:07,243 --> 00:54:09,620
Marvin.

477
00:54:09,662 --> 00:54:11,831
-A rescue.
-Well, dogs...

478
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:13,666
Dogs are cool.

479
00:54:22,675 --> 00:54:26,637
I'm sure you must have a few
questions of your own, Sam.

480
00:54:28,931 --> 00:54:31,017
Actually, just one.

481
00:54:34,353 --> 00:54:36,355
Why I never came home.

482
00:54:40,193 --> 00:54:42,987
Those nights when
I went to the office,

483
00:54:43,029 --> 00:54:46,365
I'm sure you've figured it out
by now, I was coming here.

484
00:54:47,492 --> 00:54:50,328
Human form into digital space.

485
00:54:50,369 --> 00:54:52,455
Heavy stuff.

486
00:54:54,415 --> 00:54:56,667
But I also had you.

487
00:54:56,709 --> 00:55:00,213
I had ENCOM. I couldn't
be in here all the time.

488
00:55:00,254 --> 00:55:03,007
I needed partners to help out.

489
00:55:03,049 --> 00:55:04,759
Tron and Clu?

490
00:55:05,551 --> 00:55:06,719
That's right.

491
00:55:09,388 --> 00:55:12,892
Tron was created by
Alan for the old system.

492
00:55:12,934 --> 00:55:15,102
I brought him here
to protect this one.

493
00:55:15,186 --> 00:55:17,438
Clu was my creation.

494
00:55:17,522 --> 00:55:21,359
A program designed
to create a perfect world.

495
00:55:21,400 --> 00:55:25,238
We were jamming,
man, building utopia.

496
00:55:25,321 --> 00:55:27,865
Hours in here were
just minutes back home.

497
00:55:27,907 --> 00:55:30,743
Just when I thought it
couldn't get any more profound,

498
00:55:30,785 --> 00:55:32,995
something unexpected happened.

499
00:55:33,621 --> 00:55:34,914
The miracle.

500
00:55:35,623 --> 00:55:37,583
The miracle.

501
00:55:37,625 --> 00:55:39,293
You remember.

502
00:55:40,586 --> 00:55:43,798
ISOs. Isomorphic algorithms.

503
00:55:44,590 --> 00:55:48,344
-A whole new life form.
-And you created them?

504
00:55:52,932 --> 00:55:54,433
No. No.

505
00:55:54,475 --> 00:55:58,104
They manifested, like a flame.

506
00:55:58,145 --> 00:56:01,107
They weren't really
from anywhere.

507
00:56:01,148 --> 00:56:04,068
The conditions were right
and they came into being.

508
00:56:05,111 --> 00:56:08,948
For centuries we've dreamed
of gods, spirits, aliens,

509
00:56:09,073 --> 00:56:11,117
an intelligence beyond our own.

510
00:56:11,158 --> 00:56:12,493
You seeing this?

511
00:56:12,577 --> 00:56:17,248
I found them in here.
Like flowers in a wasteland.

512
00:56:20,126 --> 00:56:22,712
Profoundly naive.

513
00:56:24,422 --> 00:56:27,174
Unimaginably wise.

514
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:31,095
They were spectacular.

515
00:56:31,137 --> 00:56:33,973
Everything I'd hoped
to find in the system,

516
00:56:34,056 --> 00:56:36,601
control, order, perfection,

517
00:56:36,642 --> 00:56:38,060
none of it meant a thing.

518
00:56:38,144 --> 00:56:39,624
I'd been living in
a hall of mirrors.

519
00:56:40,438 --> 00:56:43,149
The ISOs shattered it.

520
00:56:43,190 --> 00:56:46,819
The possibilities of their
root code, their digital DNA.

521
00:56:46,861 --> 00:56:49,322
Disease? History.

522
00:56:50,072 --> 00:56:51,741
Science, philosophy,

523
00:56:51,824 --> 00:56:56,037
every idea man has ever had
about the universe up for grabs.

524
00:56:56,120 --> 00:56:58,956
Bio-digital jazz, man.

525
00:56:59,707 --> 00:57:03,294
The ISOs, they were going
to be my gift to the world.

526
00:57:03,336 --> 00:57:05,713
So what happened?

527
00:57:05,796 --> 00:57:09,258
Clu. Clu happened.

528
00:57:12,428 --> 00:57:15,222
Your transport to the
portal is waiting for you.

529
00:57:15,306 --> 00:57:17,475
I don't like it when
you cut it this close.

530
00:57:17,516 --> 00:57:21,604
Will you stop worrying,
Tron? Everything's just fine.

531
00:57:21,687 --> 00:57:23,856
-Everything's under control.
-Flynn!

532
00:57:28,611 --> 00:57:31,197
Am I still to create
the perfect system?

533
00:57:32,740 --> 00:57:34,367
Yeah.

534
00:57:37,703 --> 00:57:38,871
It was a coup.

535
00:57:41,290 --> 00:57:42,333
Go.

536
00:57:56,889 --> 00:57:58,432
You've been corrupted.

537
00:58:08,484 --> 00:58:11,362
Why? Why?

538
00:58:14,073 --> 00:58:15,199
Flynn, go!

539
00:58:22,456 --> 00:58:25,418
Tron, he fought for me.

540
00:58:26,877 --> 00:58:29,171
I never saw him again.

541
00:58:29,964 --> 00:58:31,674
So why didn't you fight?

542
00:58:32,133 --> 00:58:34,176
-Hmm.
-He did.

543
00:58:34,260 --> 00:58:36,053
Clu fed on my resistance.

544
00:58:36,095 --> 00:58:38,848
The more I fought, the
more powerful he became.

545
00:58:39,390 --> 00:58:41,642
It was impressive, really.

546
00:58:42,226 --> 00:58:47,106
And my miracle... Clu saw
the ISOs as an imperfection.

547
00:58:47,732 --> 00:58:49,692
So he destroyed them.

548
00:58:52,903 --> 00:58:54,613
The Purge.

549
00:58:55,114 --> 00:58:59,118
-He killed them all?
-It was genocide.

550
00:58:59,702 --> 00:59:03,330
I tried to get back but I
couldn't get to the portal.

551
00:59:03,873 --> 00:59:08,335
It uses massive power and
it can't stay open forever.

552
00:59:09,128 --> 00:59:11,464
And like a safe, it...

553
00:59:11,505 --> 00:59:14,300
It can only be opened
from the outside.

554
00:59:16,260 --> 00:59:19,096
It closed on me, Sam.

555
00:59:19,638 --> 00:59:22,058
That's why I never came home.

556
00:59:29,023 --> 00:59:31,233
So the portal, it activated

557
00:59:31,317 --> 00:59:34,111
when I came in.
So it's open now.

558
00:59:34,153 --> 00:59:35,196
Not for long.

559
00:59:35,279 --> 00:59:37,907
Only one millicycle,
about eight hours.

560
00:59:37,990 --> 00:59:41,368
So we go now. Go home.
We make a run for it.

561
00:59:41,452 --> 00:59:43,621
-We get you out of here.
-Don't rush.

562
00:59:43,662 --> 00:59:45,873
What do you mean?
The portal's gonna close.

563
00:59:48,042 --> 00:59:49,668
What? What is it?

564
00:59:49,752 --> 00:59:53,839
The moment Flynn is on the Grid, Clu
will stop at nothing to obtain his disk.

565
00:59:53,923 --> 00:59:56,008
My disk is everything, Sam.

566
00:59:56,092 --> 00:59:59,553
It's the master key. The
golden ticket. The way out.

567
01:00:00,679 --> 01:00:04,183
-And not just for me.
-What do you mean?

568
01:00:04,266 --> 01:00:07,019
Our worlds are more
connected than anyone knows.

569
01:00:07,061 --> 01:00:09,313
Clu figures if I can be in...

570
01:00:09,355 --> 01:00:11,065
He can be out?

571
01:00:11,148 --> 01:00:14,735
-With my disk, it's possible.
-And then what?

572
01:00:15,361 --> 01:00:17,113
Game over.

573
01:00:17,905 --> 01:00:20,741
The guy doesn't
dig imperfection.

574
01:00:22,243 --> 01:00:24,745
What's more imperfect
than our world?

575
01:00:26,288 --> 01:00:29,625
I can't let that
happen. I won't.

576
01:00:30,042 --> 01:00:33,254
So what do we do? Nothing?

577
01:00:33,337 --> 01:00:36,298
It's amazing how productive
doing nothing can be.

578
01:00:36,382 --> 01:00:40,010
Clu's planning something.
We've known that for a while.

579
01:00:40,386 --> 01:00:41,762
Programs have been disappearing.

580
01:00:41,846 --> 01:00:44,515
There's unrest out
there, even revolution.

581
01:00:44,557 --> 01:00:48,811
If we sit tight, Clu might be
brought down from the inside.

582
01:00:48,894 --> 01:00:52,231
If the portal is closing, we can't
sit around. We have to move now.

583
01:00:52,273 --> 01:00:57,111
Tell me, what brought
you here, to the Grid?

584
01:00:57,611 --> 01:00:59,530
Alan got your page.

585
01:00:59,572 --> 01:01:02,366
I didn't send any page.

586
01:01:02,825 --> 01:01:04,076
It was Clu.

587
01:01:04,160 --> 01:01:07,079
Clu sent that page.
That's why you're here.

588
01:01:07,121 --> 01:01:10,124
This is all his design.
He wanted a new piece

589
01:01:10,207 --> 01:01:12,668
on the board to change the game!

590
01:01:12,751 --> 01:01:14,837
With you, he got more
than he ever dreamed.

591
01:01:14,920 --> 01:01:20,092
This is precisely what he wants.
Us together heading for the portal.

592
01:01:20,134 --> 01:01:24,305
It's his game now. The
only way to win is not to play.

593
01:01:26,307 --> 01:01:28,267
Well, that's a hell
of a way to live.

594
01:01:28,309 --> 01:01:29,935
But it is a way.

595
01:01:34,690 --> 01:01:36,567
We can go home.

596
01:01:38,444 --> 01:01:40,404
Don't you want that?

597
01:01:41,030 --> 01:01:46,577
Sometimes life has a way of moving
you past things like wants and hopes.

598
01:01:47,286 --> 01:01:51,999
That's great, Dad.
Keep telling yourself that.

599
01:01:57,630 --> 01:01:58,839
Good night, Sam.

600
01:02:22,071 --> 01:02:24,406
How can he be so
afraid of his own creation?

601
01:02:24,490 --> 01:02:27,660
I mean, he built Clu. Why
doesn't he just end him?

602
01:02:28,953 --> 01:02:31,038
He could, but it would
require reintegration.

603
01:02:31,121 --> 01:02:32,623
Yeah, all right.

604
01:02:32,665 --> 01:02:36,377
Flynn would never survive the event.
It would mean the end of them both.

605
01:02:36,794 --> 01:02:40,130
If he refuses to save
himself, then I will.

606
01:02:44,301 --> 01:02:46,011
How?

607
01:02:46,053 --> 01:02:48,555
I'm going through the portal.

608
01:02:48,639 --> 01:02:50,391
Clu wants Flynn's
disk, not mine.

609
01:02:50,474 --> 01:02:55,104
I'm going to find Alan and we'll
figure this thing out from the other side.

610
01:02:55,187 --> 01:02:58,649
This may be Clu's game here, but in
my world, he's gone in one keystroke.

611
01:02:58,691 --> 01:03:02,027
But I can't do anything
unless I get to the portal.

612
01:03:03,362 --> 01:03:04,488
And my guts tell me

613
01:03:04,530 --> 01:03:08,617
that you don't want to be stuck
in this place for eternity either.

614
01:03:10,786 --> 01:03:14,581
I really think you should
consider your father's wisdom.

615
01:03:15,457 --> 01:03:17,251
I have.

616
01:04:20,898 --> 01:04:22,816
There's someone I once knew,

617
01:04:22,900 --> 01:04:26,028
a program named Zuse who
fought alongside the ISOs.

618
01:04:26,111 --> 01:04:29,406
They say he can
get anyone anywhere.

619
01:04:31,116 --> 01:04:33,118
How do I find him?

620
01:04:36,038 --> 01:04:37,915
This is his sector.

621
01:04:41,210 --> 01:04:44,254
Make it there alive,
and he'll find you.

622
01:05:24,962 --> 01:05:26,588
Sam?

623
01:05:30,175 --> 01:05:31,468
Sam?

624
01:06:03,584 --> 01:06:07,546
All programs are required
to present identity disks

625
01:06:07,629 --> 01:06:09,089
at city checkpoints.

626
01:06:13,385 --> 01:06:15,971
Hey, man. It's your lucky day.

627
01:06:22,895 --> 01:06:26,023
-Any program without their disk...
-Stop him!

628
01:06:26,064 --> 01:06:28,484
...will be taken into custody.

629
01:06:30,152 --> 01:06:35,073
Any program in violation of their
function is subject to termination.

630
01:06:35,616 --> 01:06:39,077
Sam Flynn? You remember me?

631
01:06:39,411 --> 01:06:43,415
-Yeah. You gave me some advice.
-And you followed it.

632
01:06:44,833 --> 01:06:47,503
It's unfortunate we
met the way we did.

633
01:06:48,795 --> 01:06:50,172
You have a good night.

634
01:06:50,255 --> 01:06:52,758
You're looking for someone.

635
01:06:55,385 --> 01:06:57,387
What makes you say that?

636
01:06:58,263 --> 01:07:00,265
Intuition.

637
01:07:02,267 --> 01:07:06,522
Sir, the sentries downtown
have recovered Flynn's light cycle.

638
01:07:07,814 --> 01:07:11,151
We've traced it to
its point of origin.

639
01:07:36,093 --> 01:07:39,012
Prepare the light
runner, Quorra.

640
01:07:39,680 --> 01:07:42,266
We're going downtown.

641
01:08:04,621 --> 01:08:06,373
Thank you for
bringing my son to me.

642
01:08:06,456 --> 01:08:07,708
Flynn!

643
01:08:07,791 --> 01:08:10,752
You don't need to go. I've sent
him to someone we can trust.

644
01:08:10,836 --> 01:08:12,963
Quorra, there is no choice.

645
01:08:13,839 --> 01:08:16,008
I won't lose him again.

646
01:08:18,010 --> 01:08:21,221
Chaos. Good news.

647
01:09:02,387 --> 01:09:05,223
Relax. They're occupied.

648
01:09:11,897 --> 01:09:15,609
His name is Castor. If you want to
speak to Zuse, you need to go through him.

649
01:09:15,692 --> 01:09:18,362
Where's your sense
of humor, my friend?

650
01:09:18,403 --> 01:09:21,740
Programs are disappearing.
Soon none of us will be left.

651
01:09:21,823 --> 01:09:24,576
Zuse can unite the
factions, foment revolution.

652
01:09:24,618 --> 01:09:28,080
-Of course Zuse can do these things.
-Grant me an audience.

653
01:09:28,163 --> 01:09:31,416
Your enthusiasm is
intoxicating, my dear Bartik,

654
01:09:31,458 --> 01:09:34,211
but Zuse's time is precious.

655
01:09:34,252 --> 01:09:36,588
We shall see.

656
01:09:38,215 --> 01:09:40,342
I brought your boy Flynn.

657
01:09:40,425 --> 01:09:45,472
If you'll excuse me for a moment,
I have to attend to something.

658
01:09:45,555 --> 01:09:48,809
But have a drink, courtesy
of the End of Line Club!

659
01:09:49,518 --> 01:09:50,769
It is happening.

660
01:09:50,852 --> 01:09:54,064
Come, away from
these primitive functions.

661
01:09:55,273 --> 01:09:57,609
The son of Flynn.

662
01:09:57,651 --> 01:10:02,614
Of all the innumerable
possibilities, he has to walk into mine.

663
01:10:03,532 --> 01:10:05,033
Libations

664
01:10:05,117 --> 01:10:07,953
for everybody!

665
01:10:10,580 --> 01:10:14,126
I'm Castor, your host.

666
01:10:14,167 --> 01:10:16,753
Provider of any and
all entertainments

667
01:10:16,795 --> 01:10:19,423
and diversions.

668
01:10:19,464 --> 01:10:20,799
At your service.

669
01:10:23,301 --> 01:10:25,762
I'm looking for Zuse.

670
01:10:25,804 --> 01:10:28,724
Indeed. Many are.

671
01:10:28,807 --> 01:10:30,767
Where can I find him?

672
01:10:30,809 --> 01:10:34,813
This, pretty miss, is a conversation
best had behind closed doors.

673
01:10:34,896 --> 01:10:38,400
Perhaps we should
retire to my private lounge.

674
01:10:41,069 --> 01:10:44,448
I designed it myself,
you know. It's true.

675
01:10:44,489 --> 01:10:48,952
I'm stepping away for a moment, boys.
Change the scheme, alter the mood.

676
01:10:48,994 --> 01:10:53,832
Electrify the boys and
girls if you'd be so kind.

677
01:10:56,334 --> 01:10:57,794
Thank you.

678
01:10:57,836 --> 01:11:00,672
Gem. My name is Gem.

679
01:11:42,172 --> 01:11:43,882
Cozy.

680
01:13:04,504 --> 01:13:07,299
-You are Clu.
-I am Clu.

681
01:13:07,382 --> 01:13:12,178
-You will create the perfect system.
-I will create the perfect system.

682
01:13:15,682 --> 01:13:18,768
Together we're gonna
change the world, man.

683
01:13:46,171 --> 01:13:47,255
Let's move.

684
01:13:49,299 --> 01:13:50,884
Zuse has been around

685
01:13:50,967 --> 01:13:52,928
since the earliest
days of the gaming grid.

686
01:13:53,345 --> 01:13:57,515
By necessity, he has to
mind all the percentages.

687
01:13:57,557 --> 01:13:59,517
All the angles.

688
01:13:59,559 --> 01:14:01,436
So when do I meet him?

689
01:14:04,022 --> 01:14:07,442
You just did.

690
01:14:10,820 --> 01:14:14,699
After the Purge, I
needed to reinvent myself.

691
01:14:14,783 --> 01:14:17,035
Self-preservation,
you understand.

692
01:14:22,082 --> 01:14:26,711
Now, what can I do for you?

693
01:14:29,422 --> 01:14:31,466
I need to get to the portal.

694
01:14:31,549 --> 01:14:33,051
Well, it's closing quickly,

695
01:14:33,093 --> 01:14:35,762
as I'm sure you're aware.

696
01:14:35,845 --> 01:14:37,389
Tick-tock, tick-tock.

697
01:14:37,430 --> 01:14:39,724
And it's quite the journey.

698
01:14:39,766 --> 01:14:42,560
Beyond the far
reaches of the Outlands.

699
01:14:42,644 --> 01:14:47,190
Your father didn't want any programs
slipping out accidentally, did he?

700
01:14:48,566 --> 01:14:53,113
-Can you help me?
-Of course.

701
01:14:53,196 --> 01:14:56,908
But first, as a man who prides
himself on staying well informed,

702
01:14:56,992 --> 01:14:59,536
I must ask who sent you my way.

703
01:15:02,455 --> 01:15:04,666
Her name's Quorra.

704
01:15:04,749 --> 01:15:06,835
Said she met you
a long time ago.

705
01:15:07,585 --> 01:15:10,005
Indeed she did.

706
01:15:10,088 --> 01:15:11,840
Many cycles ago.

707
01:15:12,841 --> 01:15:15,593
It was a different time.

708
01:15:15,677 --> 01:15:19,597
But we're not here to relive the past.
Let's see about your future, shall we?

709
01:15:19,639 --> 01:15:22,267
We'll have to change your attire

710
01:15:22,350 --> 01:15:25,645
and you'll need a forged
disk. Not easy these days.

711
01:15:25,729 --> 01:15:27,480
And of course
you'll need transport

712
01:15:28,523 --> 01:15:31,568
to cross the Sea of Simulation.

713
01:15:42,704 --> 01:15:45,331
This is going to
be quite the ride.

714
01:15:57,844 --> 01:15:59,637
I believed in users once before.

715
01:16:01,473 --> 01:16:03,266
Playing all the angles.

716
01:16:07,771 --> 01:16:09,064
Resist!

717
01:16:17,822 --> 01:16:21,576
The game has
changed, son of Flynn!

718
01:16:37,884 --> 01:16:40,345
I met your friend.
He's fantastic!

719
01:16:40,428 --> 01:16:43,848
Behold! The son of our maker!

720
01:16:57,654 --> 01:16:59,030
Yeah!

721
01:17:08,915 --> 01:17:10,291
Yeah, yeah!

722
01:17:12,168 --> 01:17:13,419
Yeah, yeah!

723
01:17:49,789 --> 01:17:51,416
Go, go!

724
01:17:56,796 --> 01:17:58,923
Let's split, man.

725
01:18:19,152 --> 01:18:20,153
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

726
01:18:38,838 --> 01:18:40,882
A little help here maybe?

727
01:19:02,195 --> 01:19:03,488
Your disk.

728
01:19:04,489 --> 01:19:05,573
Dad, it's gone.

729
01:19:06,658 --> 01:19:07,867
It is.

730
01:19:10,662 --> 01:19:12,330
I'm sorry. I know I messed up.

731
01:19:14,499 --> 01:19:15,500
We can go back.

732
01:19:15,583 --> 01:19:18,336
-I can go back.
-No, we stay together.

733
01:19:18,378 --> 01:19:21,422
-Dad, I can do this.
-You've done enough already!

734
01:19:26,719 --> 01:19:28,763
Sam, you're really...

735
01:19:31,474 --> 01:19:33,726
You're messing with
my Zen thing, man.

736
01:19:36,312 --> 01:19:37,689
She's stable.

737
01:19:38,815 --> 01:19:42,110
-So what do we do now?
-I don't know. Nothing.

738
01:19:43,069 --> 01:19:45,029
We do nothing.

739
01:19:45,613 --> 01:19:47,156
Be still.

740
01:19:49,742 --> 01:19:51,369
Wait.

741
01:19:59,127 --> 01:20:02,005
You ever jump a freight train?

742
01:20:03,172 --> 01:20:04,215
Huh?

743
01:20:04,257 --> 01:20:07,468
We do it your way.
Full-on sprint to the portal.

744
01:20:07,552 --> 01:20:09,429
If we beat Clu there,
we have a chance.

745
01:20:09,512 --> 01:20:10,847
Let's get her out of here.

746
01:20:29,741 --> 01:20:31,534
This'll take us there.

747
01:20:58,436 --> 01:21:00,938
-Is she gonna make it?
-I don't know.

748
01:21:00,980 --> 01:21:03,649
I've got to identify
the damaged code.

749
01:21:03,733 --> 01:21:07,278
The sequencing is just
enormously complex.

750
01:21:08,404 --> 01:21:13,117
-But didn't you write it?
-Some of it. The rest of it is just

751
01:21:15,953 --> 01:21:18,498
beyond me.

752
01:21:19,749 --> 01:21:22,126
She's an ISO.

753
01:21:22,168 --> 01:21:24,629
Yeah. The last ISO.

754
01:21:26,923 --> 01:21:28,299
All this time,

755
01:21:28,383 --> 01:21:30,760
you were just protecting her.

756
01:21:30,802 --> 01:21:34,847
She's the miracle, man.
Everything I ever worked for.

757
01:21:36,224 --> 01:21:40,478
"A digital frontier to reshape
the human condition."

758
01:21:40,561 --> 01:21:43,815
I always thought that
was just a plug line.

759
01:21:43,856 --> 01:21:48,111
In our world, she could
change everything.

760
01:21:49,487 --> 01:21:51,656
Yeah.

761
01:21:53,408 --> 01:21:55,827
Check that out.

762
01:22:04,001 --> 01:22:06,129
She risked herself for me.

763
01:22:08,047 --> 01:22:10,383
Some things are worth the risk.

764
01:22:23,980 --> 01:22:25,898
Look at this.

765
01:22:28,776 --> 01:22:32,363
Now, that is impressive if
I do say so myself. Huh?

766
01:22:33,823 --> 01:22:37,034
Come on, it's gonna take a
while for her system to reboot.

767
01:22:37,076 --> 01:22:40,204
Now it's time for
you to tell me a story.

768
01:22:58,431 --> 01:23:00,725
The boy and Flynn are gone.

769
01:23:00,808 --> 01:23:04,645
I presume, Your Excellency,
they perished in the elevator.

770
01:23:08,107 --> 01:23:09,692
You presume?

771
01:23:11,819 --> 01:23:14,030
Find them.

772
01:23:18,326 --> 01:23:21,704
Icecaps are melting,
war in the Middle East,

773
01:23:21,746 --> 01:23:23,915
Lakers/Celtics back at it.

774
01:23:25,082 --> 01:23:28,252
I don't know. Rich are getting
richer, poor are getting poorer.

775
01:23:28,336 --> 01:23:31,088
Cell phones,
online dating, Wil-Fi.

776
01:23:31,130 --> 01:23:34,258
-What's Wil-Fi?
-Wireless interlinking.

777
01:23:34,300 --> 01:23:37,178
-Of digital devices?
-Yeah.

778
01:23:37,428 --> 01:23:40,681
Hmm. I thought of that in '85.

779
01:23:45,311 --> 01:23:47,438
Mom and Dad are...

780
01:23:49,190 --> 01:23:51,442
-I assume that...
-Yeah.

781
01:23:52,610 --> 01:23:53,653
Oh.

782
01:23:54,695 --> 01:23:57,073
Mac when I was 12

783
01:23:57,114 --> 01:24:00,076
and Gram five years later.

784
01:24:02,828 --> 01:24:06,707
You remember that night
when you didn't come home?

785
01:24:06,791 --> 01:24:08,000
-Well...
-You said...

786
01:24:08,084 --> 01:24:10,169
I said I'd show you the Grid.

787
01:24:12,213 --> 01:24:14,549
You should have seen
this place back then.

788
01:24:15,466 --> 01:24:20,805
I couldn't wait to show
it to you. Could not wait.

789
01:24:20,888 --> 01:24:23,432
Must have been something
before Clu screwed it up.

790
01:24:23,474 --> 01:24:25,226
No, no, he...

791
01:24:26,978 --> 01:24:29,689
He's me. I screwed it up.

792
01:24:31,148 --> 01:24:33,317
Chasing after perfection.

793
01:24:35,361 --> 01:24:39,073
Chasing after what
was right in front of me.

794
01:24:39,657 --> 01:24:41,576
Right in front of me.

795
01:24:43,452 --> 01:24:45,830
Look what you've accomplished.

796
01:24:46,163 --> 01:24:47,999
It's incredible.

797
01:24:48,040 --> 01:24:49,458
Sam,

798
01:24:50,376 --> 01:24:53,671
I'd have given it all up
for one more day with you.

799
01:25:06,809 --> 01:25:07,852
Hey.

800
01:25:08,436 --> 01:25:10,646
Remember your old Ducati?

801
01:25:10,813 --> 01:25:14,025
You kidding? Not a day goes
by I don't think about that bike.

802
01:25:14,108 --> 01:25:18,070
-Yeah, well, I'm fixing her up.
-You busted my bike?

803
01:25:18,154 --> 01:25:23,868
Twenty years in the shed, no
tarp. I mean, she needed a little love.

804
01:25:25,453 --> 01:25:27,038
How does she run?

805
01:25:27,079 --> 01:25:31,083
Well, when I'm
done, better than ever.

806
01:25:32,335 --> 01:25:34,879
Well, man, I'd like to see that.

807
01:25:36,505 --> 01:25:38,049
You will.

808
01:25:41,385 --> 01:25:42,470
Here.

809
01:25:42,762 --> 01:25:45,222
She's rebooting. Give her this.

810
01:25:45,306 --> 01:25:49,143
The old man's gonna knock
on the sky, listen to the sound.

811
01:26:15,461 --> 01:26:17,004
When Flynn entered the space,

812
01:26:17,463 --> 01:26:20,591
ah, everything changed.

813
01:26:21,133 --> 01:26:23,761
I've never seen
anything quite like it.

814
01:26:24,303 --> 01:26:26,806
The awe was

815
01:26:27,682 --> 01:26:29,100
palpable.

816
01:26:30,685 --> 01:26:32,937
-Was it?
-I presume

817
01:26:33,604 --> 01:26:36,774
our understanding
is still valid?

818
01:26:38,317 --> 01:26:40,444
Control of the city?

819
01:26:41,028 --> 01:26:44,031
A sizeable request, I know.

820
01:26:44,115 --> 01:26:46,951
But seemingly
fitting compensation.

821
01:26:47,618 --> 01:26:48,994
Don't you think?

822
01:26:50,413 --> 01:26:53,958
How long have you been
searching for this, Clu?

823
01:26:55,084 --> 01:26:57,670
About 1,000 cycles. No?

824
01:26:58,462 --> 01:27:01,590
Just imagine the
secrets it holds.

825
01:27:04,510 --> 01:27:07,471
The master key to
any and all riddles

826
01:27:08,139 --> 01:27:10,641
of the Grid, Grid, Grid, Grid...

827
01:27:13,477 --> 01:27:15,312
But there's something else, too.

828
01:27:15,855 --> 01:27:17,022
Isn't there?

829
01:27:17,106 --> 01:27:18,983
I've heard the chatter

830
01:27:19,066 --> 01:27:22,486
about this private initiative.

831
01:27:31,996 --> 01:27:35,040
I realize that our alliance is,

832
01:27:35,124 --> 01:27:36,542
at times,

833
01:27:36,625 --> 01:27:38,127
uneasy.

834
01:27:38,169 --> 01:27:40,171
But always necessary.

835
01:27:41,964 --> 01:27:43,632
You know you need me

836
01:27:43,716 --> 01:27:45,718
right where I am.

837
01:27:45,801 --> 01:27:47,261
Clu?

838
01:27:47,845 --> 01:27:50,055
Of course you're right.

839
01:27:50,806 --> 01:27:52,600
Enjoy the drink.

840
01:28:00,232 --> 01:28:02,359
End of line, man.

841
01:28:11,994 --> 01:28:15,080
Hey. It's okay.
We're safe for now.

842
01:28:15,164 --> 01:28:17,792
We're heading east
towards the portal.

843
01:28:20,503 --> 01:28:22,379
Clu has the disk.

844
01:28:23,047 --> 01:28:25,925
Once I get out, I
can shut him down.

845
01:28:28,052 --> 01:28:31,597
I should never have sent
you to Zuse. It was a mistake.

846
01:28:31,680 --> 01:28:34,183
It's okay. I've
made a few myself.

847
01:28:39,647 --> 01:28:41,273
Where is he?

848
01:28:42,233 --> 01:28:45,069
I think he's
knocking on the sky.

849
01:28:45,236 --> 01:28:47,363
And listening to the sound.

850
01:28:48,572 --> 01:28:49,990
Yeah.

851
01:28:50,574 --> 01:28:52,576
How did you find him?

852
01:29:02,086 --> 01:29:03,212
It's okay.

853
01:29:05,965 --> 01:29:07,424
I know.

854
01:29:12,638 --> 01:29:14,974
It was during the Purge.

855
01:29:16,100 --> 01:29:18,102
Clu was relentless.

856
01:29:18,435 --> 01:29:21,814
The Black Guard were
executing ISOs in the streets.

857
01:29:22,940 --> 01:29:25,734
Everyone I knew disappeared.

858
01:29:28,362 --> 01:29:30,447
Then they came for me.

859
01:29:33,158 --> 01:29:35,119
So I ran.

860
01:29:36,161 --> 01:29:39,456
A sympathetic program
smuggled me out of the city.

861
01:29:39,540 --> 01:29:42,084
But soon they had me surrounded.

862
01:29:42,126 --> 01:29:44,169
I prepared for the end.

863
01:29:44,336 --> 01:29:46,714
And just as everything
was going dark,

864
01:29:47,298 --> 01:29:50,301
I felt a hand on my shoulder.

865
01:29:52,970 --> 01:29:55,055
And when I opened my eyes,

866
01:29:56,473 --> 01:30:00,895
standing above
me was the Creator.

867
01:30:03,522 --> 01:30:05,316
Your father.

868
01:30:06,901 --> 01:30:08,569
He saved me.

869
01:30:12,823 --> 01:30:16,327
I guess you could
say I'm a rescue.

870
01:30:35,387 --> 01:30:37,181
Hell of a view.

871
01:30:37,348 --> 01:30:40,184
It used to let us know
that Flynn was here.

872
01:30:40,225 --> 01:30:42,603
It became the symbol
of something bigger,

873
01:30:42,686 --> 01:30:46,023
something better
than this world.

874
01:30:46,774 --> 01:30:49,234
I've never been
this close before.

875
01:30:50,402 --> 01:30:52,988
It's how I imagine
a sunrise to be.

876
01:30:53,030 --> 01:30:55,366
Ah, trust me. There's
no comparison.

877
01:30:58,827 --> 01:31:00,746
What's it like?

878
01:31:02,790 --> 01:31:05,250
-The sun?
-Yeah.

879
01:31:06,126 --> 01:31:08,128
Man...

880
01:31:09,713 --> 01:31:12,341
I've never had to
describe it before.

881
01:31:14,343 --> 01:31:15,552
Warm.

882
01:31:17,596 --> 01:31:19,181
Radiant.

883
01:31:21,934 --> 01:31:23,727
Beautiful.

884
01:31:49,378 --> 01:31:52,131
Get below! Move!

885
01:31:53,924 --> 01:31:56,260
This isn't supposed to be here.

886
01:32:00,514 --> 01:32:03,892
-What happened?
-A new course.

887
01:32:14,778 --> 01:32:16,196
What is this?

888
01:32:17,156 --> 01:32:18,782
Clu can't create programs.

889
01:32:19,116 --> 01:32:21,744
He can only destroy
or repurpose them.

890
01:32:22,661 --> 01:32:25,247
Repurpose them for what?

891
01:32:28,625 --> 01:32:32,463
Battalion 6, report to
Staging Area Alpha.

892
01:32:35,632 --> 01:32:37,217
He's building an army.

893
01:32:38,218 --> 01:32:39,553
Let's go.

894
01:32:39,636 --> 01:32:44,808
All high-level functions, report
immediately to combat stations.

895
01:33:10,000 --> 01:33:12,294
-Goodbye.
-Quorra!

896
01:33:12,753 --> 01:33:15,798
-What's she doing?
-Removing herself from the equation.

897
01:33:33,857 --> 01:33:35,359
Tron.

898
01:33:37,111 --> 01:33:39,196
He's alive.

899
01:33:39,822 --> 01:33:42,324
COMPUTER; Throne
ship is approaching.

900
01:33:45,202 --> 01:33:48,872
-We can't just let her go.
-No, Sam, there's another way.

901
01:33:49,540 --> 01:33:52,000
Throne ship is approaching.

902
01:34:03,220 --> 01:34:05,347
Well done, sir.

903
01:34:19,570 --> 01:34:22,072
I've never seen
anything like it.

904
01:34:22,531 --> 01:34:26,201
Humbly, sir, I know
you have greater designs

905
01:34:26,243 --> 01:34:28,871
than any of us understand.

906
01:34:30,038 --> 01:34:31,498
What does it do?

907
01:34:57,357 --> 01:34:59,276
She's gonna wind
up like one of them.

908
01:34:59,776 --> 01:35:00,986
Keep moving, Sam.

909
01:35:11,622 --> 01:35:15,459
You are a very rare
bird, aren't you, now?

910
01:35:23,634 --> 01:35:25,427
Where's your disk?

911
01:35:27,971 --> 01:35:29,806
Where is he?

912
01:35:31,725 --> 01:35:34,478
It must have been
so lonely out there.

913
01:35:35,729 --> 01:35:38,315
How tragic to be the only one.

914
01:35:40,234 --> 01:35:43,153
I've seen what users
are capable of, Clu.

915
01:35:43,946 --> 01:35:46,198
You don't belong with them.

916
01:35:51,328 --> 01:35:54,206
I have something very
special in mind for you.

917
01:35:57,751 --> 01:35:59,336
Take her upstairs.

918
01:35:59,753 --> 01:36:01,505
And find them.

919
01:36:02,214 --> 01:36:07,010
You'll have to excuse me. You arrived
just as I was preparing a little toast.

920
01:36:22,067 --> 01:36:24,027
Greetings, programs!

921
01:36:27,990 --> 01:36:31,910
Together we have
achieved a great many things.

922
01:36:32,160 --> 01:36:36,164
We have created a vast, complex
system. We've maintained it.

923
01:36:37,457 --> 01:36:39,918
We've improved it.

924
01:36:40,002 --> 01:36:43,922
We have rid it of
its imperfection.

925
01:36:45,507 --> 01:36:47,009
Not to mention

926
01:36:47,092 --> 01:36:50,387
rid it of the false deity
who sought to enslave us.

927
01:36:52,723 --> 01:36:54,933
Kevin Flynn!

928
01:36:55,976 --> 01:36:58,812
Where are you now?

929
01:37:01,523 --> 01:37:04,735
My fellow programs,
let there be no doubt

930
01:37:04,776 --> 01:37:07,362
that our world is
a cage no more.

931
01:37:07,779 --> 01:37:12,409
For at this moment, the key
to the next frontier is finally

932
01:37:12,659 --> 01:37:14,244
in our possession!

933
01:37:19,750 --> 01:37:21,710
Your disk.

934
01:37:21,752 --> 01:37:23,503
And unlike our selfish Creator,

935
01:37:23,587 --> 01:37:27,299
who reserved the privilege
of our world only for himself,

936
01:37:27,382 --> 01:37:31,053
I will make their world open

937
01:37:31,136 --> 01:37:33,388
and available to all of us!

938
01:37:36,641 --> 01:37:37,976
Yes!

939
01:37:38,477 --> 01:37:40,145
To all of us!

940
01:37:50,822 --> 01:37:52,342
He's taking all
of this with him.

941
01:37:52,824 --> 01:37:54,701
He's figured out how to do it.

942
01:37:54,785 --> 01:37:56,703
And whatever we find there,

943
01:37:56,787 --> 01:37:58,955
there our system will grow!

944
01:37:59,039 --> 01:38:02,626
There our system will blossom!

945
01:38:03,877 --> 01:38:05,420
Do this.

946
01:38:05,462 --> 01:38:08,131
Prove yourselves.
Prove yourselves to me!

947
01:38:08,215 --> 01:38:09,800
Be loyal to me!

948
01:38:10,300 --> 01:38:13,178
And I will never betray you!

949
01:38:25,732 --> 01:38:27,359
Dad, we have to get your disk.

950
01:38:27,484 --> 01:38:30,278
We gotta get to the portal.
You shut them down outside.

951
01:38:30,320 --> 01:38:33,031
Even if I make it, you won't
last in here, nor will Quorra.

952
01:38:33,115 --> 01:38:36,368
-We'll be all right. Come on.
-I'm not going home without you.

953
01:38:37,494 --> 01:38:38,787
Sam...

954
01:38:39,329 --> 01:38:41,123
The same team.

955
01:38:41,998 --> 01:38:43,417
Remember?

956
01:38:45,544 --> 01:38:47,587
I was afraid you
were gonna say that.

957
01:38:48,630 --> 01:38:50,817
Meet me on the flight deck in
five and get us some wheels.

958
01:38:50,841 --> 01:38:53,009
Wheels? What's your plan?

959
01:38:53,844 --> 01:38:56,304
I'm a user. I'll improvise.

960
01:38:57,848 --> 01:38:59,850
Maximize efficiency.

961
01:39:01,226 --> 01:39:04,146
Rid the new system
of its imperfection!

962
01:39:06,690 --> 01:39:10,277
My vision is clear,
fellow programs.

963
01:39:11,194 --> 01:39:15,365
Out there is a new world!

964
01:39:16,116 --> 01:39:18,827
Out there is our victory!

965
01:39:20,245 --> 01:39:21,788
Out there

966
01:39:23,874 --> 01:39:26,376
is our destiny.

967
01:40:10,003 --> 01:40:12,714
Identify yourself, program.

968
01:40:15,884 --> 01:40:18,970
I'm not a program.
My name is Sam Flynn.

969
01:40:42,953 --> 01:40:45,413
-Identify yourself.
-I'm taking this vehicle.

970
01:40:45,497 --> 01:40:47,415
You are not authorized.

971
01:40:49,709 --> 01:40:52,128
Right away, sir.

972
01:40:53,129 --> 01:40:56,508
Watch your step, please,
as you board the aircraft.

973
01:41:07,769 --> 01:41:09,980
Long live the users.

974
01:41:16,778 --> 01:41:19,614
Master key disengaged.

975
01:41:19,823 --> 01:41:22,242
Master key disengaged.

976
01:41:22,492 --> 01:41:26,621
I came with a girl, a
program. Where is she?

977
01:41:29,124 --> 01:41:30,834
Sam! Go!

978
01:41:57,027 --> 01:41:59,404
-Why are you here?
-We gotta get to the flight deck.

979
01:41:59,487 --> 01:42:00,780
Clu will be here any minute.

980
01:42:00,864 --> 01:42:02,699
-We'll never make it.
-Come on.

981
01:42:09,080 --> 01:42:10,457
Come on, kiddo.

982
01:42:14,044 --> 01:42:16,796
Radical, man.

983
01:42:24,554 --> 01:42:26,056
Hurry!

984
01:42:26,139 --> 01:42:27,849
Made it.

985
01:42:46,576 --> 01:42:49,663
Try and hold on to this.
You're gonna need it.

986
01:42:54,668 --> 01:42:58,338
You got this, Quorra.
It's all in the wrist.

987
01:43:13,228 --> 01:43:16,773
Light fighter 5.
Unauthorized launch.

988
01:43:37,836 --> 01:43:39,921
Death to the user!

989
01:44:04,320 --> 01:44:05,572
Head towards the light, Quorra.

990
01:44:08,450 --> 01:44:10,285
Where did you learn that move?

991
01:44:10,368 --> 01:44:12,996
ENCOM Tower.
Couple of nights ago.

992
01:44:15,498 --> 01:44:18,168
ENCOM Tower. Huh.

993
01:44:19,919 --> 01:44:21,171
Light jets.

994
01:44:21,713 --> 01:44:23,131
Here they come.

995
01:44:24,007 --> 01:44:26,468
-Sam, take the turret.
-Huh?

996
01:44:34,684 --> 01:44:37,020
Man, I'm all over this.

997
01:44:39,939 --> 01:44:41,107
Yeah!

998
01:44:50,992 --> 01:44:54,287
Yeah! One down, five to go!

999
01:45:00,001 --> 01:45:01,044
Nice.

1000
01:45:10,470 --> 01:45:12,388
We gotta split them up!

1001
01:45:32,158 --> 01:45:33,576
Come on.

1002
01:45:37,747 --> 01:45:39,833
Have a nice swim!

1003
01:45:45,922 --> 01:45:48,007
We gotta get behind them!

1004
01:45:48,591 --> 01:45:50,468
Whoo!

1005
01:45:55,807 --> 01:45:59,018
-I don't think this is a good idea.
-You're probably right.

1006
01:46:04,774 --> 01:46:06,276
He's gaining on us!

1007
01:46:37,056 --> 01:46:38,474
Yes!

1008
01:46:49,986 --> 01:46:51,029
It's jammed.

1009
01:46:56,618 --> 01:46:59,913
Tron. What have you become?

1010
01:47:04,918 --> 01:47:06,252
Oh, come on.

1011
01:47:09,422 --> 01:47:12,008
Flynn, go!

1012
01:47:15,428 --> 01:47:17,680
Rinzler! Take the shot!

1013
01:47:20,516 --> 01:47:22,268
Finish the game!

1014
01:47:30,109 --> 01:47:32,070
Roll!

1015
01:47:44,457 --> 01:47:47,210
I fight for the users.

1016
01:47:57,136 --> 01:47:59,639
That's it. It's over.

1017
01:48:00,556 --> 01:48:01,641
It's over!

1018
01:48:03,726 --> 01:48:05,561
Whoo!

1019
01:48:13,069 --> 01:48:16,239
Quorra, there's
something I need you to do.

1020
01:49:04,912 --> 01:49:06,831
Let's get you home, Dad.

1021
01:49:10,877 --> 01:49:12,211
There it is.

1022
01:49:12,795 --> 01:49:17,091
-Take her down.
-Hang on. This could be rough.

1023
01:50:09,268 --> 01:50:11,521
This is mine.

1024
01:50:16,692 --> 01:50:18,820
I had a feeling you'd be here!

1025
01:50:18,903 --> 01:50:22,740
The cycles haven't
been kind, have they?

1026
01:50:23,658 --> 01:50:25,952
Oh, you don't look so bad.

1027
01:50:27,203 --> 01:50:30,832
I did everything.
Everything you ever asked.

1028
01:50:31,374 --> 01:50:33,167
I know you did.

1029
01:50:33,209 --> 01:50:36,546
-I executed the plan!
-As you saw it.

1030
01:50:36,671 --> 01:50:41,884
You... You promised that we
would change the world together.

1031
01:50:42,218 --> 01:50:44,387
-You broke your promise.
-I know.

1032
01:50:44,637 --> 01:50:46,055
I understand that now.

1033
01:50:46,097 --> 01:50:49,559
I took this system to
its maximum potential.

1034
01:50:49,642 --> 01:50:51,811
I created the perfect system!

1035
01:50:51,894 --> 01:50:55,648
The thing about perfection
is that it's unknowable.

1036
01:50:56,774 --> 01:51:01,404
It's impossible but it's also
right in front of us all the time.

1037
01:51:01,529 --> 01:51:05,199
You wouldn't know that because
I didn't when I created you.

1038
01:51:06,951 --> 01:51:08,744
I'm sorry, Clu.

1039
01:51:10,830 --> 01:51:13,249
I'm sorry.

1040
01:51:34,937 --> 01:51:36,189
Go.

1041
01:51:49,619 --> 01:51:50,745
Clu!

1042
01:51:51,662 --> 01:51:53,956
Remember what you came for.

1043
01:52:07,970 --> 01:52:08,971
Dad!

1044
01:52:09,096 --> 01:52:10,598
You knew I'd beat you.

1045
01:52:10,723 --> 01:52:13,809
And still you did
all this? For him.

1046
01:52:19,941 --> 01:52:21,192
No.

1047
01:52:26,781 --> 01:52:28,074
No!

1048
01:52:28,157 --> 01:52:29,492
Why?

1049
01:52:31,160 --> 01:52:32,578
He's my son.

1050
01:52:38,918 --> 01:52:39,961
Go!

1051
01:52:45,800 --> 01:52:46,884
Dad!

1052
01:52:53,432 --> 01:52:55,601
Sam! It's time!

1053
01:52:55,851 --> 01:52:57,019
No!

1054
01:52:57,353 --> 01:53:00,147
Sam, it's what he wants.

1055
01:53:02,191 --> 01:53:04,110
I'm not leaving you!

1056
01:53:04,527 --> 01:53:06,028
Take her!

1057
01:53:17,456 --> 01:53:19,041
Yes!

1058
01:53:46,736 --> 01:53:48,404
Goodbye, kiddo.

1059
01:54:19,727 --> 01:54:21,604
No!

1060
01:55:32,508 --> 01:55:34,343
Al?

1061
01:55:38,764 --> 01:55:40,599
You paged me?

1062
01:55:41,100 --> 01:55:42,768
Yeah.

1063
01:55:43,519 --> 01:55:45,855
I need you at ENCOM at 8:00 a.m.

1064
01:55:47,773 --> 01:55:49,316
What about the board?

1065
01:55:50,943 --> 01:55:52,862
You're chairman now.

1066
01:55:55,197 --> 01:55:57,658
I'm taking the
company back, Alan.

1067
01:56:01,704 --> 01:56:02,955
Oh, and...

1068
01:56:04,206 --> 01:56:05,875
You were right.

1069
01:56:07,543 --> 01:56:09,003
About what?

1070
01:56:10,629 --> 01:56:12,214
About everything.

1071
01:56:37,072 --> 01:56:38,407
What's next, Sam?

1072
01:56:44,163 --> 01:56:47,583
I guess we're supposed
to change the world.

1073
01:56:51,587 --> 01:56:54,340
Come on. I wanna
show you something.

1074
02:05:05,664 --> 02:05:06,665
English - US - SDH
